t/","size":41744,"stargazers_count":5620,"watchers_count":5620,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1204,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1060,"license":{"key":"gpl-2.0","name":"GNU General Public License v2.0","spdx_id":"GPL-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/gpl-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTg="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["closember","code-quality","hacktoberfest","linter","pep8","static-analysis","static-code-analysis"],"visibility":"public","forks":1204,"open_issues":1060,"watchers":5620,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Originally reported by: **Brianna Laugher (BitBucket: [pfctdayelise](http://bitbucket.org/pfctdayelise), GitHub: @pfctdayelise?)**\n\n---\n\nRe R0924 'A class implements some of the special methods for a particular protocol, but not all of them'\n\nwhich was introduced in http://www.logilab.org/ticket/104420 / 6416aab & issue #25 / commit 50a1da7\n\nI don't have a problem with checks for magic methods being used to avoid false R0903 (\"too few public methods\") alerts, and the check for context managers makes sense. However I'm not too convinced about the \"sin\" of implementing some container related magic methods without implementing all of them.\n\nWith reference to http://docs.python.org/dev/library/collections.abc.html ,\n\nIf you have registered a class as a Sequence and only implemented `__len__` and not `__getitem__`, it makes sense to warn about that. But what exactly is the harm of `__len__` without `__getitem__` or vice versa? (And the docs even say something with only `__len__` is Sized, rather a poorly implemented `__getitem__`)\n\nI think if the user hasn't registered their class with an ABC, pylint can't know very reliably what is intended.\n\nIf these checks are used, I think they should correspond to the docs (both in required magic methods and names - \"bad container\" should actually be \"bad sequence\").\n\n---\n- Bitbucket: https://bitbucket.org/logilab/pylint/issue/52\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/52/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/52/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]